  "changelog": {
    "sha256": "5f9c8b949ef67d14c83d18ed639c90f98e0f131ad1f31b9435efb5ddcba0bff3",
    "text": "## [0.6.2] - 2026-11-02\n\n### Changed\n\n- Linux AppImage: Mumcord's window and extra windows (What's new, packet inspector) open much faster. Each window spent seconds rescanning the system's GStreamer plugins, twice on systems where /usr/lib64 points to /usr/lib\n\n### Fixed\n\n- \"What's new\" now opens on the notes of the version you are running, followed by the older releases; a release used to open on the previous version's notes, and a section called \"Unreleased\" or notes of newer versions could show up\n- \"What's new\" has its notes built into the app, so it no longer needs to load them and cannot get stuck loading\n- Plugin icons in the strip under the channel list are now centred in their buttons and drawn larger.\n- The disconnect menu of the hang-up button now opens above the button instead of running off the bottom of the window, and \"Switch voice\" has an icon\n\n### Internal\n\n- Updated dependencies: `libloading` 0.9, `sha1` 0.11, the Rust and npm minor and patch updates and the cargo-deny GitHub Action; `async-executor` moves off a yanked release so the dependency audit passes again"
  },
